Everything outside the kernel lives in its own repository and is checked
out here as a git submodule, the way Linux and the programs that run on
it are separate projects.  .gitmodules in the top directory lists them:

  toolchain   Leonix_toolchain: lxasm.py, the assembler for the virtual
              machine, used by "make check" and by coreutils
  coreutils   Leonix_coreutils: sh, ls, cat and the other programs that
              the kernel packs into /bin

Each submodule is pinned to the commit the kernel was last built and
tested with.  To fetch them with a new clone:

  git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/w3ngzv/Leonix.git

or, in an existing clone:

  git submodule update --init

To move a submodule to a newer commit, check that commit out inside it,
build and test the kernel, then commit the submodule path here.
